ave data unchanged.\n   - Else, locate the bad data bit via `p1 - log2(p1) - 2` and flip it.\n   On failure it truncates `output` back to its starting length.\n\n5. **`hecc_decode`** — Rejects truncated inputs (`len % 16 == 1`), processes full 16-byte blocks, then handles a final partial block by repacking the trailing parity byte into position 15 of a zero-padded 16-byte buffer before invoking the impl.\n\nNo `unsafe`, no FFI, no external crates; only safe Rust standard library operations."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":970,"cache_read_input_tokens":31960,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":970,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9197576d-5155-4bb8-8598-5403a8f76c37","uuid":"6f770042-75e6-43cd-849b-85e570476a7c"}
